--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (4/4 key facts kept) ---
I found a half-crown under Mr. Hale's desk, and was pleased. Bert and I spoke about the docks, and he told me he was working there. I pawned the watch, and cried a little. Bert gave me 3s. 6d., and I went to market.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks she is a truthful little girl.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He considers Mr. Thomas a sensible man.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (4/4 key facts kept) ---
I spoke with Joan about what she did today, and found that she went to the station to meet Aunt Jane. I searched for the half-crown, which she dropped, but could not find it. I talked with Walter Thomas about Consols, and was glad to hear of a reduction in the rate of interest, because Consols will then be a better investment for small savings. Walter paid me my week's wages, and Edith and I talked of the housekeeping money.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks Mr. Arthur Hale a steady, hard-working young man.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 14th of March, 1930 (0/1 key facts kept) ---
I was glad to hear of the proposed reduction of the rate of interest on Consols, because Consols will then become a better investment for persons of small income.

